  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\qt0009_ef51dc5e4e92.png\"><br>\r\nIn the given figure, 1 represents isobaric, 2 represents isothermal and 3 represents adiabatic processes of an ideal gas. If $\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{1}, \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{2}, \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{3}$ be the changes in internal energy in these processes respectively, then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{1}     < \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{2} < \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{1}>\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{3}     < \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{1}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{2}>\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{1}>\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{2}>\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0009_c8f55d448de5.png\"><br>\r\n$\\Delta \\mathrm{T}_{1}=\\mathrm{T}_{0}$\r\n$\\Delta \\mathrm{T}_{2}=0$\r\n$\\Delta \\mathrm{T}_{3}=-\\mathrm{ve}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{1}>\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{2}>\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{3}$"
  }
